			<ns0:title type="html">Silicon Valley is falling in line with Trump’s attempt to rename AI</ns0:title>
			<ns0:link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1009406/silicon-valley-is-falling-in-line-with-trumps-attempt-to-rename-ai" />
			<ns0:id>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1009406</ns0:id>
			<ns0:updated>2026-10-11T14:33:56-04:00</ns0:updated>
			<ns0:published>2026-10-11T14:33:56-04:00</ns0:published>
			<ns0:category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="AI" /><ns0:category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="News" /><ns0:category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Policy" /><ns0:category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Politics" />
							<ns0:summary type="html">When President Donald Trump announced his plans to rebrand artificial intelligence as "super intelligence," you'd be forgiven for being skeptical that it would catch on. While most of the broader population is sticking with AI, some of Silicon Valley's most powerful are falling in line and trying to</ns0:summary>
			
